Can't you talk to your system administrator?

> I have installed zlib 1.2.11 (and other necessary libraries) in my
> home directory.
> Problem is the cluster has an older zlib library (1.2.4) and R does
> not accept that. How can I force configure to look in my
> home/[username]/packages/lib for zlib?
> 
> 
> [username at hpcc3 R-3.4.0]$ ./configure --
> prefix=/home/[username]/packages --with-x=no --with-readline=no --
> includedir=/home/[username]/packages/include
> ?libdir=/home/[username]/packages/lib

Set environment variables:

CPPFLAGS=-I<includedir> \
LDFLAGS=-L<libdir> \
./configure

Martyn

